 341: Mac at `192.168.101.166`, not the already-used `rohansharma` home and not a new
 342: machine. This is the chosen interpretation of “clean machine” because Lima
 343: machine state, iolbox host data, launcher attestations, caches, downloads, and
 344: quarantine state are all per-user, while the known physical Apple Silicon,
 345: macOS, and Homebrew Lima installation remain available. A different Mac would
 346: add an owner-supplied-target dependency that M6 does not currently have.
