 397: Status meanings:
 398: 
 399: - **PASS**: every sub-observation in the criterion was executed successfully
 400:   against the workflow-produced archive on real Apple Silicon where the
 401:   criterion calls for hardware.
 402: - **NOT RUN**: no meaningful attempt was made, including unavailable access or
 403:   missing owner-supplied test input.
 404: - **FAIL**: it was attempted and any required sub-observation failed or could
 405:   not be completed. A later code/doc fix does not turn FAIL into PASS until the
 406:   corrected workflow artifact is rerun through that criterion.
