 541: ## 8. Acceptance criteria
 542: 
 543: The implementation result copies this table and assigns exactly one status to
 544: each row.
 545: 
 546: | # | Criterion required for PASS | Required evidence |
 547: |---|---|---|
 548: | 1 | CI executes launcher vet/unit tests, compiles Darwin-selected tests, and cross-builds `CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64`; the workflow-produced binary also starts/diagnoses on the real Mac. | Green CI job/log, workflow artifact provenance, `file` output, real-Mac command transcript. |
 549: | 2 | The release workflow emits exactly `iolbox-macos-arm64.tar.gz` plus its outer checksum; the archive has exactly §2.2, all internal checksums pass, its native payload is byte-identical to the same run's `build-linux` payload, and a second identical pack has the same hash. | Workflow log/artifacts, two hashes, extracted manifest, payload hash comparison on the Mac. |
 550: | 3 | A fresh supported Apple Silicon user with only Lima as the separately installed runtime prerequisite reaches the rendered GUI using the browser-downloaded archive and one documented `./iolbox start`. | Clean-state inventory, browser download, launcher/HTTP/browser/service/canary evidence on hardware. |
 551: | 4 | Browser download quarantine is recorded before mutation and the exact documented, narrow first-run Gatekeeper procedure succeeds without signing, notarization, global disablement, or automatic clearing. | xattr exit/output for archive/directory/binary, Gatekeeper screenshot/transcript, successful first run. |
 552: | 5 | The `curl` path is independently downloaded, checksum-verified, extracted, xattr-checked, and successfully used on the Mac; presence or absence of quarantine is reported rather than assumed. | curl transcript/version, separate hashes/listing/xattrs, real command result. |
 553: | 6 | A real owner-supplied x86_64 IOL image runs in a saved two-node lab and passes bidirectional traffic through the shipped artifact; i386 and arm64-native IOL are not advertised as supported. | Rendered GUI/hello evidence, console transcripts, last complete ping summaries, saved-lab proof. |
 554: | 7 | `./iolbox upgrade` from the `cf19f2f` baseline archive to the candidate preserves host and guest images/labs, hostid/hostname, exact iourc hash, Lima machine identity, and pinned guest kernel; the saved lab reloads and passes traffic afterward. | Complete before/after identity table and post-upgrade browser/traffic evidence. |
 555: | 8 | Plain launcher removal leaves the stopped VM and data intact and re-extraction recovers the same lab; the separately warned destructive sequence deletes only the named VM/data and is demonstrated last. | Lima/data listings before removal, after removal, after recovery, and after destructive cleanup. |
 556: | 9 | `docs/INSTALL.md`, archive README, provider docs, third-party notice, maintainer release doc, and draft release notes consistently name Lima, actual supported macOS/profile and guest/kernel matrix, Rosetta-amd64, x86_64-IOL-only, unsigned/Gatekeeper, loopback security, upgrade, and uninstall boundaries. | Exact published draft text/archive notice reviewed against the workflow artifact and real observations; no unsupported capability claim. |
