 608: ### 7.5 Authenticated `curl` download, quarantine, and payload identity
 609: 
 610: The repo is public, but the draft assets require authentication. The owner
 611: supplies `IOLBOX_GH_TOKEN` securely; use `set +x`, never echo it, and exclude
 612: credential entry/environment dumps from evidence. Obtain and record the two
 613: release asset IDs and Linux workflow artifact ID from GitHub metadata, then:
 614: 
 615: ```sh
 616: mkdir "/Users/<clean-user>/Downloads/iolbox-m6-curl"
 617: cd "/Users/<clean-user>/Downloads/iolbox-m6-curl"
 618: test "$(pwd)" = "/Users/<clean-user>/Downloads/iolbox-m6-curl"
 619: set +x
 620: curl --fail --location --header "Accept: application/octet-stream" \
 621:   --header "Authorization: Bearer ${IOLBOX_GH_TOKEN}" \
 622:   --header "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
 623:   --output "iolbox-macos-arm64.tar.gz" \
 624:   "https://api.github.com/repos/rohan-punj/iolbox/releases/assets/<archive-asset-id>"
 625: curl --fail --location --header "Accept: application/octet-stream" \
 626:   --header "Authorization: Bearer ${IOLBOX_GH_TOKEN}" \
 627:   --header "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
 628:   --output "iolbox-macos-arm64.tar.gz.sha256" \
 629:   "https://api.github.com/repos/rohan-punj/iolbox/releases/assets/<checksum-asset-id>"
 630: curl --fail --location --header "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
 631:   --header "Authorization: Bearer ${IOLBOX_GH_TOKEN}" \
 632:   --header "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
 633:   --output "iolbox-linux-artifact.zip" \
 634:   "https://api.github.com/repos/rohan-punj/iolbox/actions/artifacts/<linux-artifact-id>/zip"
 635: ```
 636: 
 637: Record response headers with authorization redacted, `curl --version`, file
 638: types, and asset metadata; require a valid gzip/tar and ZIP rather than HTML.
 639: Record archive xattrs and exit statuses, verify the outer checksum, extract to
 640: `extract/`, verify internal `SHA256SUMS`, and record directory/binary xattrs.
 641: Extract the Linux workflow artifact to `trusted-linux/`, locate its
 642: `SHA256SUMS-ci.txt`, and compare by exact basename:
 643: 
 644: ```sh
 645: cd "/Users/<clean-user>/Downloads/iolbox-m6-curl"
 646: payload="$(find "extract/iolbox-macos-arm64" -maxdepth 1 -type f -name 'iolbox-server-*.tar.gz' -print)"
 647: test -n "$payload"
 648: test "$(find "extract/iolbox-macos-arm64" -maxdepth 1 -type f -name 'iolbox-server-*.tar.gz' -print | wc -l | tr -d ' ')" = "1"
 649: base="$(basename "$payload")"
 650: test "$(awk -v b="$base" '$2 == b || $2 == "*" b {n++} END {print n+0}' "trusted-linux/SHA256SUMS-ci.txt")" = "1"
 651: expected="$(awk -v b="$base" '$2 == b || $2 == "*" b {print $1}' "trusted-linux/SHA256SUMS-ci.txt")"
 652: printf '%s\n' "$expected" | grep -Eq '^[0-9A-Fa-f]{64}$'
 653: actual="$(shasum -a 256 "$payload" | awk '{print $1}')"
 654: test "$actual" = "$expected"
 655: printf 'workflow_run=%s payload=%s expected=%s actual=%s PASS\n' "<run-id>" "$base" "$expected" "$actual" | tee "payload-identity-mac.txt"
 656: ```
 657: 
 658: Apply §4 only when the candidate binary is actually quarantined. This curl
 659: extraction is the sole upgrade input in §7.4.
