 151: `SHA256SUMS` uses paths relative to `iolbox-macos-arm64/`, sorted bytewise and
 152: generated after permissions are normalized. The release also attaches
 153: `iolbox-macos-arm64.tar.gz.sha256` next to the archive so a user can verify the
 154: download before extraction. That outer checksum is not inside the archive.
 155: Checksums published in the same unsigned release provide corruption/tamper
 156: detection after publication, not cryptographic publisher identity; the docs
 157: must not describe them as a substitute for signing.
