 163: ### 2.3 Repeatability and payload identity
 164: 
 165: Add one manifest as the allow-list for the archive. Every manifest source must
 166: be a regular, non-symlink file. The packer must fail on a missing manifest
 167: member, an unexpected staged member, more or fewer than one native payload
 168: tarball, a launcher which is not Mach-O arm64, or a payload whose hash does not
 169: match an explicit trusted `--payload-sha256` input. The release job derives
 170: that input by selecting exactly one well-formed checksum line whose basename
 171: exactly matches the payload from the same run's `SHA256SUMS-ci.txt`; duplicate,
 172: missing, mismatched-basename, or malformed lines fail the job.
 173: 
 174: Packing runs on Ubuntu with GNU tar. Validate `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` as a
 175: non-negative integer; stage twice into independently created directories; set
 176: `LC_ALL=C`; sort the complete member list bytewise; normalize directories to
 177: 0755, `iolbox` to 0755, other files to 0644, numeric uid/gid to zero, and mtime
 178: to `@${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH}`; then create a fixed pax-format stream with
 179: `--pax-option=delete=atime,delete=ctime` and pipe it through `gzip -n`. The
 180: release-layout test requires the two independently staged archives to be
 181: byte-identical and have identical SHA-256 values. The GitHub tag, native
 182: payload filename, release metadata, and checksums carry version identity; the
 183: launcher has no embedded version claim or new version-stamp feature in M6.
 184: 
 185: The pack operation uses the equivalent of this concrete recipe for each fresh
 186: stage (with `stage-members.txt` generated by `LC_ALL=C sort` from the exact
 187: manifest-expanded tree):
 188: 
 189: ```sh
 190: LC_ALL=C gtar --create --format=pax --owner=0 --group=0 --numeric-owner \
 191:   --mode='u+rwX,go+rX,go-w' --mtime="@${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH}" \
 192:   --pax-option=delete=atime,delete=ctime --no-recursion \
 193:   --files-from=stage-members.txt -C "$stage" | gzip -n > "$output"
 194: ```
