 801: 1. **M4 remains PARTIAL and is out of scope.** Only items 1 and 6 were proven
 802:    on hardware; items 2 and 7 have unit-tested fixes not hardware-reconfirmed;
 803:    items 3, 4, 5, and 8 were not attempted. M6 does not proactively execute or
 804:    close that backlog. Because M6 packages and runs the cumulative M1–M5
 805:    product, an unresolved M4 defect may surface naturally in the clean install,
 806:    lab, upgrade, or uninstall run. Root-cause and record it. Fix M6 packaging/
 807:    docs defects in scope; do not turn the session into an M4 backlog hunt. If
 808:    the defect blocks an M6 criterion, that criterion is FAIL until resolved and
 809:    rerun.
 810: 2. **M5 is fully PASS; M4 is the only inherited incomplete phase.** M5
 811:    criterion 2 passed on `noble-builder-vm` as recorded in the current M5
 812:    handoff/result. M6 has no amd64 non-Mac exception, inference, or acquisition,
 813:    and no M6 step depends on that criterion remaining open.
 814: 3. **Hardware access is a gate, not an implementation assumption.** §0 requires
 815:    a genuinely fresh account with SSH plus either agent-controlled interactive
 816:    desktop/browser access or owner-executed GUI evidence handoff. If it is not
 817:    met, rows 1–8 are NOT RUN wherever their Mac evidence cannot be produced.
 818:    `rohansharma`, `sudo -iu`, and HTTP-only evidence are not silent fallbacks.
 819: 4. **Quarantine varies by browser, settings, extraction path, and macOS.** A
 820:    browser may auto-extract, propagate quarantine differently, or Gatekeeper
 821:    may present a different UI than expected. The plan records all layers before
 822:    mutation and forbids synthetic xattrs. The candidate `xattr -d` procedure is
 823:    deliberately file-scoped, but it must be replaced everywhere if hardware
 824:    proves a different user action is the successful path.
 825: 5. **Unsigned provenance remains limited.** Internal and outer hashes detect
 826:    mismatch but, when hosted beside the unsigned artifact, do not authenticate
 827:    the publisher. Release and install docs must say the artifact is unsigned;
 828:    M6 has no hidden signing/notarization work.
 829: 6. **Exact-payload coupling is a release risk.** Rebuilding the native payload
 830:    independently in `build-macos`, selecting “newest”, or allowing multiple
 831:    tarballs could ship different bits from the native-systemd artifact. The Mac
 832:    job therefore consumes and hash-compares the exact `build-linux` output from
 833:    the same run.
 834: 7. **Draft download authentication is required even though the repo is
 835:    public.** Draft assets are collaborator-only until publication. Reconfirm
 836:    visibility before the session, keep the clean browser authenticated, use
 837:    exact GitHub REST asset IDs for curl, and keep the token out of history,
 838:    tracing, saved headers, and environment dumps. HTML is a failed download.
 839: 8. **External downloads can fail.** Lima and the pinned guest image are not in
 840:    the archive. A moved image URL, unavailable mirror, stale Homebrew Lima
 841:    bottle, or Rosetta share warning can block clean provisioning. Keep the
 842:    structural canary and digest refusal intact. `brew upgrade lima` is not
 843:    remediation for a stale same-version bottle; the known action is
 844:    `brew reinstall lima`, performed by the user outside iolbox.
 845: 9. **The 8 GB Mac is resource-constrained and already has other-user VMs.**
 846:    Stop only owner-approved reusable machines if needed and never touch
 847:    `iol22`. Use 1024 MB per IOL node and record host memory pressure so a
 848:    resource failure is not mislabelled as archive corruption.
 849: 10. **Browser automation has protocol traps.** WebSocket evidence needs the
 850:    HTTP session cookie plus same-origin `Origin`; consoles replay their ring
 851:    buffer; and after supervisor restart the app may need a full page reload.
 852:    Carry these M3/M5 facts forward before calling a product failure.
 853: 11. **Lima configuration has a known quoting trap.** If qualification
 854:     diagnostics must inspect or reproduce a `limactl --set` operation, yq map
 855:     keys in the expression must remain quoted. Do not “simplify” the locked
 856:     template or a working launcher-generated expression while debugging the
 857:     archive. Record the rendered per-machine Lima YAML before blaming the
 858:     provisioner.
 859: 12. **Shared-worktree contamination is possible.** Earlier phases observed a
 860:     concurrent session changing and committing files in the same worktree.
 861:     Recheck branch/HEAD/status at every handoff, preserve the pre-existing
 862:     `docs/m6-session-logs/` tree, and stage exact paths only.
 863: 13. **Schedule confidence is low.** The master estimate is 1.5–2 focused days,
 864:     including one clean-machine pass. Every earlier Mac phase exceeded its
 865:     estimate once real hardware exposed defects that CI/static review missed.
 866:     Reserve an uninterrupted genuine clean-account hardware pass plus time for
 867:     at least one corrected workflow rebuild/rerun; CI-green is only the entry
 868:     gate, not schedule completion.
 869: 
 870: ## 10. Explicit non-goals
 871: 
 872: - M4 backlog closure or proactive M4 regression hunting.
 873: - Code signing, notarization, entitlements, a `.app`, `.dmg`, Homebrew formula,
 874:   package installer, or automatic Gatekeeper/quarantine changes.
 875: - Installing, upgrading, reinstalling, or uninstalling Lima for the user.
 876: - A guest disk or bundled hypervisor.
 877: - Tauri/Rust shell repair or release packaging.
 878: - i386/i86bi enablement, arm64-native IOL, native-arm64 supervisor/VPCS,
 879:   FEX/qemu-user, or any other M7 work.
 880: - Changes to launcher lifecycle, sync, ports, GUI, supervisor, native payload,
 881:   or guest provisioning behavior unless the later implementation session finds
 882:   a defect directly preventing an M6 acceptance criterion and separately
 883:   obtains the appropriate scope decision.
 884: 
 885: ## 11. Estimate and handoff condition
 886: 
 887: Retain the master estimate of 1.5–2 focused days as the no-defect engineering
 888: estimate: roughly half a day for CI/packer/release integration, half a day for
 889: docs/notices and workflow dry run, and at least half to one full day for the
 890: fresh-account browser/curl/lab/upgrade/uninstall sequence. This is not a promise
